    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7.41, Ment Hyg L",
    "lawSection": "Mental Hygiene Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4534\n\nSPONSOR: BROUK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to the geriatric\nservice demonstration program to promote mental health and home care\ncollaboration\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRequires the Commissioner of the Office of Mental Health to identify\nbarriers that would prevent providers from accessing the Geriatric\nDemonstration Program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new subdivision (d) to section 7.41 of the mental\nhygiene law to require the Commissioner of the Office of Mental Health\nto identify barriers that would prevent providers from accessing the\nGeriatric Demonstration Program.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill allows the state to further facilitate the goals of the Geria-\ntric Services Demonstration Program by addressing regulatory, financial\nand systemic barriers to collaboration with mental health providers and\nhome care providers.\n\nIt will address major barriers to the program's goal of providing\ncomprehensive, person-centered care within a collaborative model, that\nsupports the total range of patient needs.\n\nAddressing financial, procedural and systemic barriers to effective\ncollaboration within the geriatric service demonstration program will\nassist in deepening the collaborative partnerships between mental health\nproviders and providers of home care and help better serve patient\nacross the care continuum.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: S8745 (Carlucci) Referred to Rules/A6566B (Gunther) Third Reading\nRules Calendar.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNo cost to the state or localities. Anticipate savings to the state from\nfurther promotion of the collaborative health-mental health effort and\nspecific goals of maintaining health and averting hospitalizations,\nemergency episodes and long-term institutionalization.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
